  "title": "Fix string formatting for PathAccessError on scope and non-standard paths",
  "instruction": "Ensure that `PathAccessError` can always be converted to a string or formatted into an error message without raising an exception (such as `TypeError`), even when the error originates from a `Scope` access or involves non-standard path objects.\n\nWhen formatting the error message for a `PathAccessError`, if the path cannot be resolved or looked up as a standard path, the exception should gracefully fall back to a readable string representation rather than crashing during `str(exc)` formatting. Standard `Path`-based error messages must continue to format correctly."
}
